  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "Depth intervals of the FWB-306 core collected 2015-06-10; workbook by Xiaoqin Wu (Chakraborty Lab, LBNL), 2015-08-24. pH, nitrate and organic carbon cover FWB306-02 to FWB306-07 (3 to 18 ft); moisture covers all eight intervals"
   }
  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "pH and nitrate were measured by Alex Aaring; the workbook gives only the mean and standard deviation of each. The standard deviations are consistent with three replicates: where the nitrate standard deviation is exactly the square root of 3 times the mean (FWB306-05, FWB306-07), one replicate of three was above zero"
   }
  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "Nitrate is mg per kg of sediment. The nitrate means include replicates read as zero. Nitrate of FWB306-06 is 0 with standard deviation 0 in the workbook and is stored as below detection (blank concentration and standard deviation, below = true); the workbook gives no detection limit"
   }
  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "Organic carbon is percent of the sediment. It is a separate measurement from the total organic carbon of the UGA soil test (hazen_sediment_soil_properties_fwb306_2015)"
   }
  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "Moisture is by freeze-drying: mass lost as percent of the wet sediment mass, (before - after) / (before - bag). FWB306-02 to FWB306-07 were weighed as two portions (replicate 1 and replicate 2); FWB306-01 and FWB306-08 as one. These values are separate from, and do not agree with, the moisture of the UGA soil test: FWB306-03 and FWB306-04 lost about 0.2 percent of their mass here, and the UGA test found 30 and 18 to 20 percent"
   }
  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "Not stored: the workbook's sulfate and moisture summary columns, which are the UGA soil test values already in hazen_sediment_extractable_fwb306_2015_v2 and hazen_sediment_soil_properties_fwb306_2015; and the bag and sediment weights"
   }
  },
  {
   "value_type": {
    "term_name": "comment",
    "oterm_ref": "ME:0000011",
    "oterm_name": "comment"
   },
   "value": {
    "scalar_type": "string",
    "string_value": "Source: ENIGMA Google Drive, 1506_CoreSummary.xlsx, sheets FW306 summary and FW306 moisture"
   }
  }
 ],
